module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GlobalTypesUnderComparison
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalOnCover.Coherence
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ToposPullbackGlobalPresentation
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.ModuleTypesOnSite
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Topos.LocalizedSpecialCocontinuous
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Local types of modules are intrinsic, through a special cocontinuous functor

Stacks 03DM asserts that each of the eight local conditions of Stacks 03DL on a sheaf of modules
on a ringed site depends only on the associated ringed topos.  The source proves it by the route
of Section 03DG: a morphism of ringed topoi which is an equivalence is, after replacing the sites,
induced by a *special cocontinuous* functor `u : C ⥤ D` of sites, and the condition is compared
across the restriction of modules along `u`.

This file carries out that route for the clauses (1) locally free, (2) finite locally free,
(3) locally generated by sections, (6) quasi-coherent and (8) coherent.  It is a
*specialisation*, not the tag: the restriction of modules along a special cocontinuous functor
is one equivalence of ringed topoi among others, and the statements below are the ones the
reduction of Stacks 03DO to a morphism of ringed sites consumes.  The clause for an arbitrary
equivalence of ringed topoi is proved for (1), (2), (3), (6) and (8) in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalTypesUnderEquivalence` and for (4), (5) and
(7) in `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ModuleTypesUnderEquivalence`.

## The comparison that is carried

Throughout, `G : C ⥤ D` exhibits `(C, J)` as a dense subsite of `(D, K)` and is cocontinuous —
jointly the hypotheses of a special cocontinuous functor, `Stacks.IsSpecialCocontinuous` — and
`R` is a sheaf of rings on `(D, K)`.  The restricted structure sheaf is
`Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.ringRestriction J K G R` and the restriction of modules is
`Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.moduleRestriction J K G R`, which is the equivalence of topoi of the
source read on modules.  Each statement below is an `iff` between the condition for a module on
`(D, K)` and the condition for its restriction to `(C, J)`; since every sheaf of rings and every
sheaf of modules on the subsite is, up to isomorphism, such a restriction, that is the assertion
that the condition is intrinsic.

No fullness or faithfulness of `G` is asked for by any clause, which is what makes them
applicable to the special cocontinuous functors Stacks 03CR produces: those are asserted to be
dense subsite inclusions and nothing more, and a special cocontinuous functor need not be
faithful, since the topology of the site being replaced need not be subcanonical.  The
localization of the inclusion is a dense subsite inclusion all the same
(`Stacks.Sites.overPost_isDenseSubsite`), which is what the clauses (1), (2), (3) and (6) run
on; the clause (8), coherence, runs instead on
`Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.isFiniteType_pushforward₀_iff`, whose descent step asks only for the
*local* fullness that `Functor.IsDenseSubsite` already carries.

The geometric input is in
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Topos.LocalizedSpecialCocontinuous`: the localized Comparison
Lemma `Stacks.LocalizedDenseSubsite.sliceEquivalence`, its further restriction
`Stacks.LocalizedDenseSubsite.sliceRestriction`, and the covering transport
`Stacks.LocalizedDenseSubsite.forall_exists_cover_iff`.  What is left here, for each clause, is
the global condition of Stacks 03DE that the local condition is built from, transported along
those two functors; that is the content of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GlobalTypesUnderComparison`, which proves every
global condition both preserved and reflected by a fully faithful coproduct-preserving functor
matching the structure sheaves.

The clause (8), coherence, is the exception: it is not a condition on the restrictions of the
module to the members of a covering family, so the covering transport does not reach it.  It is
two instances of the sectionwise finite-type condition of Stacks 03DL (5), and those are carried
across the restriction of modules directly, by
`Stacks.DenseSubsiteModules.isFiniteType_pushforward₀_iff`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isLocallyFreeOnSite_iff`: the special cocontinuous case of
  Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (1), local freeness.
* `Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_iff`: the special cocontinuous
  case of Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (2), finite local freeness.
* `Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff`: the special
  cocontinuous case of Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (3), local generation by sections.
* `Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isQuasicoherentOnSite_iff`: the special cocontinuous case
  of Stacks 03DM for the clause 03DL (6), quasi-coherence.
* `Stacks.Sheaves.SpecialCocontinuous.isCoherentOnSite_iff`: **Stacks 03DM for the clause
  03DL (8)**, coherence.

## Implementation notes

The two sites live in a common pair of universes, as explained in the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Topos.LocalizedSpecialCocontinuous`: the covering families of
Stacks 03DL are indexed in `Type (max u v)` for the universes of the site, so transporting one
to the other needs those universes to agree.

The forward implication of each clause goes through
`Stacks.LocalizedDenseSubsite.sliceRestriction`, which is *not* fully faithful — it restricts
along `Over.map` first — so only the preservation halves of the global comparisons are available
for it; the reverse implication goes through `Stacks.LocalizedDenseSubsite.sliceEquivalence`,
which is an equivalence, so the reflection halves are available there.  This asymmetry is the
source's own: its first paragraph refines a covering and only preserves the global condition,
while its second paragraph uses the equivalence of the localized topoi in both directions.

